{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver never reached the pickup point on the platform's own telemetry. Across 79 fixes spanning 23:10:40 to 23:23:40, the closest the driver's device ever came to the pin at Clarke Quay was 623.57 m (mean 823.00 m, worst 1625.98 m). The arrival radius for this trip's zone class, LARGE_VENUE, is 120 m. There is not a single fix inside it: qualifying_fix_count is 0. POL-NS-01 limb (b) requires the gps_trace to place the driver inside the POL-NS-02 geofence at or before the 'arrived' event, and it does not, at any point in the 15 minutes before the 23:24:10 cancellation. Limb (b) fails and the fee is not chargeable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even setting arrival aside, POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails: the dwell is zero. The trace records no in-geofence interval at all - qualifying_fix_count is 0, run_count is 0, longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec is 0.0, and accumulated_dwell.accumulated_sec is 0.0 - against a minimum_dwell_sec of 300 for LARGE_VENUE. The 9 minutes of 'wait' in the trip record is a record of driving, not of waiting: the driver's distinct speeds on this trace run from 28.1 to 30.6 kph over 2.11 km of travel. With limb (b) and limb (c) both broken, POL-NS-01 cannot carry the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived' marker at 23:15:10 is a false marker on both independent triggers in POL-NS-05. Distance: the trace's minimum distance across the whole trip is 623.57 m, so at the marker the driver was at least 623 m out, more than double the 300 m trigger. Motion: the same trace records sustained speeds of 28.1 to 30.6 kph, well above the 15 kph trigger, i.e. the vehicle was travelling, not holding at a kerb. The waiting clock must therefore be recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix - and there is none. Under POL-NS-05(ii) the cancellation fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and this trip must be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver in the ruling's referrals list.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 gives the same result independently: the effective in-geofence dwell, computed under POL-NS-02 and corrected under POL-NS-05, is 0 seconds against the 300 second minimum for LARGE_VENUE - a shortfall of 300 seconds. POL-NS-06(ii) is explicit that a shortfall refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded. The one qualification, limb (i) accumulation of separate in-geofence intervals, is unavailable twice over: there are no separate intervals to accumulate (run_count 0), and there is no traffic advisory on file at all. EV-ADVIS-00627-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0, and a MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable rather than exonerating anyone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627", "EV-ADVIS-00627-01", "EV-FARE-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot fall back on POL-NS-03. That clause reaches only a driver who was stationary for the required dwell at a point outside the arrival radius but not more than 400 m from the pin. The 400 m ceiling is measured from trip_record.pickup, and this driver's minimum distance was 623.57 m - he was never inside it. There are no stationary fixes within 400 m, no venue_id on the pickup to corroborate a same-venue mislocation, and no chat message from either party naming an entrance, block or bay. This is not a wrong-entrance case; it is a driver who was not at the venue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627", "EV-CHAT-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was at the pin, and was there for the whole window. The rider track carries 64 fixes from 23:14:40 to 23:24:07, every one of them qualifying, with a mean distance of 12.90 m from the pin and a maximum of 17.62 m - comfortably inside the 150 m rider presence radius for LARGE_VENUE, and identical in count to rider_qualifying_fix_count (64). The driver's statement that 'the passenger wasn't visible' is therefore contradicted by the platform's own device telemetry of the rider's device.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00627", "EV-DPROF-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On POL-NS-04, limbs (b) and (c) are met squarely. Limb (b): the rider messaged at 23:16:40; the driver's last and only message was at 23:16:30, and the driver posted nothing after it, so no reply came within 120 seconds. The only in-app call in trip_record.in_app_calls was placed by the RIDER at 23:15:40, not by the driver, and was answered for 40 seconds - so the call limb of (b) is not triggered against the rider either. Limb (c): 64 of 64 rider fixes within 150 m. On limb (a), I put the rider's position candidly: the rider's message is 'no, you cancel', which coordinates the resolution of the pickup but is not one of the enumerated location statements. The enumerated list reads as illustrative of 'locating or coordinating', and the rider was in fact at the pin; but if the Judge reads limb (a) as confined to the listed location content, this claim falls away and nothing else in the case depends on it, because POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 each dispose of the fee on the GPS trace alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627", "EV-GPS-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record is impaired and I disclose it: EV-TRIP-00627 carries weight_multiplier 0.4 with issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT (MAJOR), the pre-pass having found that its arrived_at of 23:15:10 and its wait_time_min of 9.0 are contradicted by the GPS positions over the same interval - the trace places the vehicle about 750 m from the pin throughout the claimed in-geofence wait. Under POL-GEN-02(1) I name the impairment rather than present it as clean. Its effect is limited: the deciding fact here, how far the driver was from the pin, rests on EV-GPS-00627, which is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and on the rider track in the same artifact. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is the maximum of the weights on the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, so the cap is 1.0 and the 0.70 escalation floor is not engaged. The trip record's contradicted figures are the only support for the charge, and at 0.4 they cannot alone carry a finding for the driver under POL-NS-08.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00627", "EV-GPS-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "This case should be decided, not escalated. POL-NS-09(b) requires two admissible artifacts contradicting each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence AND no clause resolving the conflict. Here a clause does resolve it: POL-NS-02 makes arrival a GPS geofence test and POL-NS-05 is drafted precisely to decide, from the trace, whether an arrival marker is false. The resolution is one-directional and leaves no open question. The repeat-behaviour and abuse triggers are also absent on the profiles: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) does not fire; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(d) does not fire; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming branch cannot fire either, at 1 termination against 110 completed trips in 30 days.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00627", "EV-DPROF-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays at 80 percent of the cancellation fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. POL-NS-01 fails at limbs (b) and (c), and POL-NS-05(ii) and POL-NS-06 each direct independently that on a false marker or a shortfall the fee is refunded with no compensation. The fare_breakdown's own derived block computes a driver_compensation of 4.80, but that figure is conditional on a fee that was never chargeable, and it must not be emitted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00627", "EV-GPS-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own message is an admission against his written statement. At 23:16:30, one minute after he marked 'arrived', he wrote 'car problem, you cancel' - the words of a driver who could not perform the trip and wanted the rider to absorb the cancellation, not of a driver who had arrived and could not park. His counterparty statement says there was no parking so he circled; the trace shows circling at 28 to 30 kph between 623 m and 1626 m from the pin, with no stationary interval inside the geofence and no advisory on file to make holding position lawfully impossible. The trip was in substance terminated by the driver for his own reason, which is not any of the three reason codes POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises, and limb (d) additionally requires termination at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed - a moment that never came.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00627", "EV-GPS-00627", "EV-ADVIS-00627-01", "EV-TRIP-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount in issue is clean and the refund is the whole of it. The fare_breakdown charges a cancellation_fee of SGD 6.00 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. That reconciles with fee_schedule: the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee (6.00) is 6.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect and no reason to discount the figure. Under POL-GEN-03 the filing party is the RIDER and the contested amount is 6.00, so a full refund returns the entire contested sum, with no driver compensation to net against it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00627", "EV-TRIP-00627"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
